   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT permitting the village board of the village of Southampton to provide\nhealth insurance coverage for enrolled members of the Southampton Village\nOcean Rescue",
    "basePrintNo": "S5742",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5742-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5742\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act permitting the village board of the village of Southampton to\nprovide health insurance coverage for enrolled members of the Southamp-\nton Village Ocean Rescue\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation recognizes the work and commitment of the Southampton\nVillage Ocean Rescue by polluting the village of Southampton to extend\nhealth insurance coverage to enrolled members.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Provides that once the village of Southampton adopts a resol-\nution designating the Southampton Village Ocean Rescue as an emergency\nrescue and first aid squad, they may further be permitted to extend\nhealth insurance coverage for enrolled members of the squad and their\nfamilies. The total cost of participation shall be borne by the volun-\nteers. .\n\nSection 2. Sets for the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFounded in April 2018, the Southampton Village Ocean Rescue (SVOR)\nresponds to emergencies in the ocean and bay throughout the village of\nSouthampton. They are dedicated to making expeditious and safe water\nrescues year round at all unprotected beaches in Southampton village.\n\nEach month SVOR trains in different locations coordinating with numerous\nemergency agencies to be prepared for a multitude of aquatic emergen-\ncies. They work with the town and village lifeguard agencies as well as\nthe police and fire departments and consistently adapt to new protocols\nto ensure proper rescue techniques that best protect the victims and\nrescuers. SVOR rescuers are ocean lifeguard and CPR certified. They\npromote water safety and educate the public the dangers of rip currents.\n\nIn 2022, the state legislature enacted a special act for the New York\nState to recognize the critical lifesaving functions and services\ncarried out by SVOR by the adoption of a resolution by the town board as\nan emergency rescue and first aid squad, under section 209-b of the\ngeneral municipal law (chapter 419 of the laws of 2022). Now designated,\nmembers may utilize green emergency lights when on route to rescue\ncalls.\n\nTo further recognize SVOR's valuable services and bolster recruitment\nand retention efforts, this legislation will permit the village of\nSouthampton to provide SVOR members and their families with health\ninsurance coverage. Those volunteers choosing coverage in the village's\nplan will bear the total coast of participation. Currently, subdivision7\nof section 92-1 of the general municipal law extends this benefit to\nSVOR's emergency responder counterparts in the volunteer fire and volun-\nteer ambulance services.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTBD.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
